    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0306" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg204"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Commission/826: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Switzerland (Wilson), at
                        Geneva</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-24T10:00:00-05:00">February 24, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>75. Your 122, February 22, 7 p.m.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d191-f1"/> You may in
                    your discretion tell Drummond in confidence that I am assuming that upon being
                    informed of your receipt of such a letter and after examination by me of text, I
                    shall be able to reply promptly and favorably and make his letter and my reply
                        public.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d191-f2"/> Please obtain his authorization for
                    my thus, in such event, making text of his letter public.<anchor n="26"
                        xml:id="d191-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d191-f1" n="24" xml:id="d191-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d191-f2" n="25" xml:id="d191-f2-content">
                <p>For texts of Drumraond’s letter and the Secretary’s reply, see telegrams No. 125,
                    February 24, 1933, 7 p.m., from the Minister in Switzerland, and No. 78,
                    February 25, 6 p.m., to the Minister in Switzerland, <ref
                        target="frus1931-41v01#pg_114"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >i</hi>, pp. 114</ref> and <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_115"
                    >115</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d191-f3" n="26" xml:id="d191-f3-content">
                <p>The Minister in Switzerland replied as follows: “Drummond much pleased and
                    authorizes you to make public text of his letter” (793.94 Commission/836).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
